# InstaSupply console configuration (docs/CLIENTS.md §8.3). Copy to `.env.local` to override locally.
#
# VITE_API_URL: origin of the API, `https://host[:port]`, no trailing slash and no `/api/v1`.
# - `npm run dev:frontend` without it: `http://<page host>:4000`.
# - `vite build` refuses to run without it (vite.config.ts), so a production bundle always names its API.
# - On Railway: VITE_API_URL=https://${{backend.RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN}} (passed to the Docker build as an ARG).
# Not a secret: it ends up in the JavaScript bundle.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
